James requested a story for his 5-year-old son that aligns with his interests in scary themes like vampires and monsters, while being suitable for an early reader. He expressed frustration with the overly sweet nature of typical early reader books. He desired a structured 4-page book featuring a bad guy protagonist, emphasizing short words and repetition for his son. I proposed a narrative with four pages, each containing a well-written short segment for James and a simple, repetitive section for his son, ensuring the story concludes effectively within the specified length.
